Fighting styles are captured as choices but not processed into a dedicated field or applied as character modifications. This makes it difficult to track fighting styles and apply their mechanical effects.

## Current State

- Fighting style choices stored in `ChoiceData` with source \"class\"
- No dedicated `fightingStyle` field on `Character` struct
- No mechanical effects applied (e.g., Defense fighting style should give +1 AC)
- No validation that fighting style is appropriate for class

## Expected Behavior

During draft-to-character conversion:
1. Process fighting style choice into dedicated character field
2. Apply fighting style bonuses where applicable
3. Validate fighting style against class-available options
4. Handle multiple fighting styles for multiclass characters

## Acceptance Criteria

### Data Structure Changes
- [ ] Add `fightingStyle string` field to `Character` struct (optional field)
- [ ] Add `FightingStyle string` field to `Data` struct for persistence
- [ ] Update `LoadCharacterFromData()` to populate fighting style field

### Fighting Style Processing
- [ ] Process fighting style choice from `shared.ChoiceFightingStyle`
- [ ] Store fighting style ID in character field
- [ ] Only process for classes that get fighting styles (Fighter, Ranger, Paladin)

### Mechanical Effects Application
- [ ] Apply Defense fighting style (+1 AC when wearing armor)
- [ ] Apply Dueling fighting style (+2 damage when wielding one-handed weapon with no other weapons)
- [ ] Document other fighting style effects for future implementation
- [ ] Create framework for fighting style effect application

### Validation Integration
- [ ] Validate fighting style choice against class options
- [ ] Ensure only appropriate classes can select fighting styles
- [ ] Prevent duplicate fighting style selections (unless multiclass allows)

### Testing
- [ ] Test Fighter with Defense fighting style (AC bonus)
- [ ] Test Fighter with Dueling fighting style
- [ ] Test non-fighting classes don't get fighting styles
- [ ] Test validation of invalid fighting style choices
- [ ] Test multiclass characters with multiple fighting styles

